diff --git a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
index 6bddff1..17a6dc9 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
@@ -96,3 +96,46 @@ __Request:__
 __Response:__
 
 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
+## `POST /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions`
+
+Registers a web push subscription so notifications that land in the user's tray are also pushed
+to that device. Only the current user can register their own devices.
+
+The subscription is what the browser hands over from the push service. Re-registering an
+endpoint replaces its keys, so a browser that subscribes again doesn't leave a stale
+subscription behind.
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `endpoint` | string | Yes | The push service URL to send pushes to |
+| `p256dh_key` | string | Yes | The user's public ECDH key, used to encrypt the payload |
+| `auth_key` | string | Yes | The user's authentication secret, used to encrypt the payload |
+
+__Request:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "push_subscription": {
+    "endpoint": "https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send/...",
+    "p256dh_key": "BEnP3B6MuUvBQv9T3OFDVLOcgyFJklqQmXWJ9wZL3XbVpWQb5pWqVQ9eYvY5zZz1W0mOaQ8tS0Xe0y2r7zXQ8mU",
+    "auth_key": "aBcDeFgHiJkLmNoPqRsTuV"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` on success, `403 Forbidden` when registering for someone else, and
+`422 Unprocessable Entity` when the subscription is missing a key.
+
+Pushes carry the title and body shown in the tray, and open the card they are about:
+
+```json
+{
+  "title": "RE: Layout is broken",
+  "body": "The text is overflowing the container.",
+  "url": "https://fizzy.example.com/897362094/cards/12",
+  "tag": "card_03f5v9zo9qlcwwpyc0ascnikz"
+}
+```
